From b056db334225754509c499b43fbe5cb1903595eb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dd6ds <dd6ds@eclipso.de>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 07:43:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] d/control: accept galera as alternative contacts backend

With the runtime backend selection the service works with either
qtcontacts-sqlite or the galera (address-book-service) backend, so do
not force qtcontacts-sqlite onto devices that only use galera.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PCCLepF6vdmVFK5L6Hvm95
---
 debian/control | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/debian/control b/debian/control
index 333e0f5..1c7e0f4 100644
--- a/debian/control
+++ b/debian/control
@@ -22,7 +22,7 @@ Architecture: any
 Multi-Arch: same
 Depends:
  bluez-obexd,
- libqt5contact5-plugin-sqlite,
+ libqt5contact5-plugin-sqlite | qtcontact5-galera,
  liblomirihistoryservice0,
  ${shlibs:Depends},
  ${misc:Depends},
-- 
2.43.0

